  "result": "Subcommands now pick up their own entry from `default_map`. The full suite passes (1907 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed).\n\n- **Fix:** In `src/click/core.py`, a child context now uses `parent.default_map.get(info_name)` instead of copying the parent's whole map.\n- **Test:** I added `test_default_map_subcommand` to `tests/test_defaults.py`. It covers a subcommand, a nested group, a missing key, a flat map with no subcommand key, and `context_settings`.\n- **Changelog:** I added an \"Unreleased\" entry at the top of `CHANGES.md`. Move it if you track unreleased changes somewhere else.\n\nThis changes behaviour for anyone who relied on the old inheritance. A flat `default_map={\"port\": 5}` no longer reaches subcommands. They need `{\"sub\": {\"port\": 5}}`, which is what the docs describe.",
